# `push_batch_within`'s early exit, inverted to stop on the productive attempt.
#
# Real: stop at the first attempt that moves nothing, because a second attempt
# against an unchanged ring can only find the same answer. Inverted: stop at the
# first attempt that moves something — which returns the identical count, since
# single-threaded there is never more than one productive attempt anyway.
#
# The published total cannot see this. The consumer's length cannot see it. What
# separates the two is one more refusal, and a refusal costs a record — see S7.
# The detector runs a budget of three where the real loop spends two attempts
# and the inverted one spends a single attempt, and reads the iterator, where
# that difference is the only place it shows.

id: S8
crate: ring_poll
file: src/lib.rs
round: 2026-08-30
round-failures: 1
detector: push_batch_within_spends_a_second_attempt_after_a_productive_first

--- from
    if moved == 0
--- to
    if moved != 0   // PROBE ONLY — G12, was `==`
--- end
